# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of platform checkout settings.
# A CRLF shebang line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails on Linux/WSL with a
# cryptic "bad interpreter" or "$'\r': command not found" error - exactly the
# failure mode scripts/verify-neon-qemu.sh would hit if a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true were allowed to convert it.
*.sh text eol=lf
